WEBVTT

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:10.920
"AUGUST 8, 2095"
"ICE PILLARS BREAK JUST BEFORE
THE WOMEN'S ROOKIE EVENT FINAL"

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.640
Rookie Event,
Women's Ice Pillars Break Final!

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.970
It's just about to start!

00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.730
Miyuki, I can finally take you on.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.660
Honoka, I'm going to give it my all, too.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:47.380
The place is packed!

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:52.710
Well, those two have rocked this arena,
and now they're going head-to-head!

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:55.970
I hear that people from
the military are here, too.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.010
And the one who set
the table for all this acclaim is

00:00:58.010 --> 00:01:00.350
this single high school student
sitting here. Who knew?

00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:03.350
Wouldn't you rather be by Miyuki's side?

00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:05.100
Yes. Of course.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.600
You're really not shy to admit it, huh?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:11.020
Ever heard of something
called "sister complex"?

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:14.690
I don't see how rooting for a family member
makes me someone with a siscon.

00:01:14.690 --> 00:01:19.570
Wait, did you hear that?
This boy is being defiant! Oh dear!

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:23.700
He's a basket case.
Probably no hope of recovery.

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:29.040
I don't think there's any point in whispering
about the person between you, do you?

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:34.760
An all-First High final.
Both have Tatsuya Shiba as their engineer.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.510
This will be an important match,
a showcase of his abilities, right, Masaki?

00:01:39.510 --> 00:01:43.970
The annual dance party on the last night
of the Nine Schools Competition...

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.980
Oh, Ms. Shiba, how badly
do I want to dance with you.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:48.270
Masaki?

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.980
Are you sure you're feeling okay?

00:01:49.980 --> 00:01:53.320
Yes. I really don't want
to miss this match.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.070
Neither do you, right?

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:57.150
Miyuki Shiba...

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:01.160
I'll be going up against her
in the Official Mirage Bat Event.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:04.830
What kind of fight
will she put up in this final?

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.290
I wonder why Shizuku said
she wanted to compete against Miyuki.

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:09.120
What?

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:13.380
Even if I were 100%,
I wouldn't want to take on Miyuki...

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:15.760
since I don't think I'd have a chance.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:19.220
Then, maybe it means Shizuku thinks
she does have a chance of beating her.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.300
What?

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.680
After all, no one knows better than Shizuku
herself how much more powerful Miyuki is.

00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:29.100
So, her desire to take her on anyway
probably means she thinks maybe she can.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.520
Shizuku...

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:35.280
And now, the moment you've been waiting for...
The players are entering the arena!

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.590
Shizuku, good luck!

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.650
Brother...

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:18.400
Would you mind putting this on me?

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:22.320
I suppose you can't very well favor
one of us over the other...

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.870
can you?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.030
Fine.

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:37.670
This is all I need to feel empowered.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:39.170
Let's go, Shizuku.

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:42.090
This is you and me playing for keeps!

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.550
Miyuki...

00:03:43.550 --> 00:03:47.930
I'm going to unleash all the results
of my training into this match!

00:05:39.080 --> 00:05:40.590
Resonance Destruction!

00:05:40.590 --> 00:05:43.000
Shizuku's mom's specialty!

00:05:52.510 --> 00:05:54.600
So, Miyuki's using Inferno?

00:05:54.600 --> 00:05:57.560
Two big moves clashing right off the bat.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.980
No matter how powerful Inferno may be...

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:01.940
the ice pillars are protected
by data fortification

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:03.780
that can block changes in temperature.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:06.650
There's no way
she can raise this temperature.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:11.530
Resonance Destruction is a spell
that causes the entire field to oscillate.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.080
I'm going to stop the oscillation...

00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.160
before she can summon Resonance!

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:20.540
You stopped the oscillation
before it could reach the resonance point.

00:06:20.540 --> 00:06:22.540
Just what I'd expect of you, Miyuki.

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:27.590
You cast data fortification
over all of the ice and blocked Inferno.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:30.720
To think that you did that
while also casting Resonance Destruction...

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:33.010
That was masterful, Shizuku.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:36.640
But that's not enough to defeat me!

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.150
Even if she can block
a phenomenon-rewriting spell,

00:06:41.150 --> 00:06:46.230
she can't prevent the ice from melting
due to the effects of the heated air around.

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.200
Shiba had that all thought out, too.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:52.120
What about you, Kitayama?

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.910
At this rate, it's all going to melt!

00:06:55.910 --> 00:07:01.370
Unbelievable! I guess Shizuku doesn't have
a chance against Miyuki, after all!

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:08.260
I can't reach her pillars at this rate.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.220
Impressive, Miyuki.

00:07:10.220 --> 00:07:12.010
In that case...

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.140
Shizuku, what's that?

00:07:22.230 --> 00:07:25.070
"JULY 19, 2095"
"15 DAYS BEFORE THE
NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION"

00:07:25.400 --> 00:07:28.360
It's no good. At this rate...

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:31.780
I just don't think
I have a chance against Miyuki.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:37.540
I know that only someone deluded
would hope to defeat Miyuki.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:41.210
But if I get the chance to face off
with her no-holds-barred,

00:07:41.210 --> 00:07:46.000
I want to master a technique
that's either equal or better!

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.550
I had no idea
you were taking this that seriously.

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:51.130
Fine.

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:54.090
In that case, there is one approach.

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:55.640
What's that?

00:07:55.640 --> 00:08:01.890
I'd suggest you use this specialized CAD
simultaneously with your generalized CAD.

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:03.560
That's just crazy!

00:08:03.560 --> 00:08:05.980
If I were to use two CADs at the same time,

00:08:05.980 --> 00:08:10.190
the Psions would interfere with each other
and I couldn't cast a decent spell!

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:12.400
I know it will be difficult.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.990
And I don't believe
that just anyone can pull it off. But...

00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:18.990
you can do it, Shizuku.

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:23.460
I'm convinced that you can.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:26.130
I can see why Honoka gets so carried away.

00:08:26.130 --> 00:08:27.000
What?

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:28.460
No, no.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:29.960
It's nothing.

00:08:32.090 --> 00:08:33.970
I'm going to use it now...

00:08:33.970 --> 00:08:35.470
Tatsuya!

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:38.560
What? She's using two CADs at once?

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:42.600
Surely not!

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.270
Kitayama...

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:47.900
I can use Spirit Magic
more or less on autopilot,

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:51.480
so I'm able to focus
on using a Modern Magic CAD.

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:53.860
But two Modern Magic CADs
at the same time...

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:55.740
Is that even possible?

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.030
The simultaneous use of two CADs

00:08:58.030 --> 00:09:02.120
is an advanced technique
requiring absolute control of the Psions.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:08.880
Does this mean you've mastered
my brother's specialty, Shizuku?

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:10.300
I know...

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:13.760
just how hard you've worked
until now, Shizuku.

00:09:13.760 --> 00:09:16.680
I know you can do it! You can!

00:09:24.890 --> 00:09:26.600
Phonon Maser?

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:29.770
All right!

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:33.780
This is the first time I've ever
seen Miyuki's ice being melted!

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:37.610
No one else even scratched them
in the prelims!

00:09:37.610 --> 00:09:39.120
Wow!

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.280
Shizuku!

00:09:41.280 --> 00:09:44.660
You've got this, Shizuku! You can win!

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.460
Not only is she using
two CADs simultaneously,

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.790
but she's also using the advanced
Oscillation-type spell, Phonon Maser.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.550
Neither of them are easy to wield.

00:09:53.550 --> 00:09:57.340
But I'm sure she has
Tatsuya Shiba's support.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:01.100
That's the result
of her determination to win this match.

00:10:01.100 --> 00:10:03.430
She knows
she doesn't measure up to Shiba,

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:07.690
yet she still didn't give up
and refined a technique to win.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:12.770
Just a little more. I can do this!

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:18.280
Shizuku... Is this what my brother
called "your resolve"?

00:10:18.530 --> 00:10:21.200
"JULY 20, 2095"
"14 DAYS BEFORE THE
NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION"

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:23.830
What? Shizuku said that?

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.660
Yes. She was full of resolve.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:32.000
I don't believe it.
Shizuku said she wanted to beat me?

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:37.670
Wanting to compete against a strong
opponent is like a magician's instinct.

00:10:37.670 --> 00:10:42.930
Wanting to play for keeps against you,
someone her own age with unparalleled skills,

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:44.760
is something I can understand.

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:45.680
So...

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:52.520
I'm going to lavish as much support as I can
on Shizuku as her engineer.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:55.530
If that's what my brother's telling me...

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.110
then does it mean she's that strong?

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:02.240
Needless to say, I'm pouring the best
of the technology I have to offer on you, too.

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:06.240
I just want you to know
that you won't be able to beat Shizuku...

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.540
unless you go full throttle.

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:13.750
Just as I thought, these emotions...

00:11:13.750 --> 00:11:17.170
I may have done Shizuku a disservice.

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:20.630
I knew that two weeks
wasn't going to be enough.

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:23.350
Brother, you've been going all out
to support Shizuku

00:11:23.350 --> 00:11:27.350
over a limited time
so that she could win.

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:29.640
And Shizuku, for her part...

00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.900
In that case...

00:11:31.900 --> 00:11:35.860
I should show you the courtesy
of responding with all my heart and soul!

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:36.730
It's coming!

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:39.110
I'm jealous of you!

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:41.320
Of your powers and your techniques!

00:11:41.320 --> 00:11:42.950
And Shizuku, that's why...

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:44.870
I don't want to...

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.410
lose to you!

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.580
What's that?

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.710
Wide-range Freezing Magic, Niflheim!

00:11:57.710 --> 00:11:59.550
What kind of a demonic realm are we in?

00:11:59.550 --> 00:12:05.800
She's going to neutralize the Phonon Maser
with that liquid nitrogen mist!

00:12:05.800 --> 00:12:07.430
I'm not going to let you do that!

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:10.930
I'm going to use data fortification
before the Phonon Maser's effects fizzle out,

00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:12.810
and maintain the status quo!

00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:18.270
Sorry, but that's naïve of you, Shizuku.

00:12:27.990 --> 00:12:30.160
She stopped the ice from melting.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:36.000
But I don't believe that's the only reason
Shiba activated Niflheim.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.630
Is that what she's doing?

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:51.470
That's right, your data fortification is working
on the pillars that were already there

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:54.230
but not on the newer deposits.

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:55.150
In other words,

00:12:55.150 --> 00:13:00.690
it has no effect on the drops and puddles
of liquid nitrogen that remain there!

00:13:00.690 --> 00:13:02.650
It's over now!

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:14.960
The liquid nitrogen on the water's surface
has vaporized thanks to Inferno's heat.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:17.130
It's expanded at a rate of...

00:13:17.130 --> 00:13:19.250
700 times!

00:14:01.210 --> 00:14:03.800
Winner of the Women's
Ice Pillars Break Rookie Event...

00:14:03.800 --> 00:14:08.180
Miyuki Shiba of First High School!

00:14:19.850 --> 00:14:21.940
"AUGUST 8, 2095"
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION - END OF DAY SIX"

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:36.160
Shizuku? I'm coming in.

00:14:46.670 --> 00:14:48.380
U-Um...

00:14:48.380 --> 00:14:50.470
Welcome back, Honoka.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:52.390
Uh, yeah.

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:55.350
Congratulations on winning
the Battle Board Event.

00:14:55.350 --> 00:14:56.930
Thanks.

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.810
Sorry about your event.

00:14:59.810 --> 00:15:01.060
Yeah.

00:15:01.060 --> 00:15:04.360
I'm sorry that I couldn't
keep our promise.

00:15:04.360 --> 00:15:07.570
Oh, please! Don't worry about...

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:10.910
I never thought I'd win.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:12.030
But...

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:14.580
But I was totally helpless!

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:17.330
When there were so many points at stake!

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:19.370
Shizuku!

00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:26.590
I really wanted to win.

00:15:36.510 --> 00:15:38.350
You're going to get wet.

00:15:38.350 --> 00:15:40.270
I don't care.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:41.270
But...

00:15:41.270 --> 00:15:45.520
I don't care!

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:49.570
I really wanted to win, Honoka!

00:15:49.570 --> 00:15:52.200
Yeah.

00:15:52.200 --> 00:15:54.120
I wanted to win!

00:15:57.740 --> 00:15:59.620
Hey, wanna go down for some tea?

00:15:59.620 --> 00:16:02.000
I think I'm a little hungry.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.080
Okay.

00:16:07.750 --> 00:16:10.260
This is way too awkward!

00:16:10.260 --> 00:16:13.550
Honoka, congratulations on winning.

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:17.510
Congratulations, Honoka.

00:16:17.510 --> 00:16:20.850
Oh, um, thank you so much!

00:16:20.850 --> 00:16:22.770
Tatsuya, is it okay if we join you?

00:16:22.770 --> 00:16:23.600
Huh?

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:25.230
Sure. Of course.

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.520
Huh?

00:16:30.530 --> 00:16:33.030
A-Are you sure about this?

00:16:33.030 --> 00:16:35.490
We're celebrating
the winner and the runner-up.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:38.580
So this is on me.

00:16:38.580 --> 00:16:40.580
Then I'm not going to be shy.

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.920
Hey, um...

00:16:50.920 --> 00:16:54.800
It was all thanks to you
that I won, Tatsuya!

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:56.760
Thank you so much!

00:16:56.760 --> 00:16:59.760
I only helped a little.

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:02.270
I didn't do right by you, Shizuku.

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:03.850
What do you mean?

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:09.320
Normally, it should've been a closer match,
but I made a bad judgment call.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:13.240
It was too much to ask you to master
Phonon Maser in just two weeks.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:16.990
No, you didn't do anything wrong, Tatsuya.

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:21.450
In the first place, I wouldn't even have had
a way to counterattack without it.

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:24.080
I should be apologizing to you.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:27.880
I also feel bad for you, Miyuki,
for not being a more worthy opponent.

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:29.670
You're wrong about that.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:32.380
I was truly taken aback
during that match.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:37.050
Brother, so you seriously meant
to set me up to lose, didn't you?

00:17:37.050 --> 00:17:41.100
I did my best for both of you. That's all.

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:42.350
Really...

00:17:42.350 --> 00:17:45.190
Don't you love your little sister?

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:47.060
But if I'd cut any corners...

00:17:47.060 --> 00:17:49.940
then you would've really been furious.

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:54.860
Who knew we'd ever see
this side of you, Tatsuya?

00:17:54.860 --> 00:17:55.820
Hey!

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:59.280
What's this? You four
are celebrating without us?

00:17:59.280 --> 00:18:02.870
No fair! Let us join the party, too!

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.830
Shizuku, you were amazing!
You looked so cool!

00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:09.380
Even though I lost?

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:10.960
It's not about winning or losing!

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:14.260
Seeing you go all out in battle
was fabulous!

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:16.510
Respect!

00:18:16.510 --> 00:18:17.760
Thanks.

00:18:17.760 --> 00:18:22.010
Tatsuya, I'm counting on you
for my Mirage Bat match tomorrow.

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:27.390
Right. I'll get your CAD adjusted
by morning along with Honoka's.

00:18:28.060 --> 00:18:32.440
Now I can finally reap the benefits
of your expertise. I'm expecting a lot.

00:18:32.440 --> 00:18:35.820
All right! Honoka and Subaru
will give us a one-two finish...

00:18:35.820 --> 00:18:38.200
so we can celebrate tomorrow, too!

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:39.950
Yeah!

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:47.750
Day Seven of the
Nine Schools Competition will start

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.500
"AUGUST 9, 2095"
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION - DAY SEVEN"
"MIRAGE BAT ROOKIE EVENT QUALIFYING ROUNDS"

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.500
with the Rookie Events for Mirage Bat!

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:50.380
"AUGUST 9, 2095"
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION - DAY SEVEN"
"MIRAGE BAT ROOKIE EVENT QUALIFYING ROUNDS"

00:18:49.500 --> 00:18:50.380
In this event...

00:18:50.380 --> 00:18:54.550
players will aim for the hologram balls
projected in midair, use magic to leap up,

00:18:54.550 --> 00:18:58.220
smash them with their sticks
and earn the most points!

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:11.650
What's going on here?

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.860
My body couldn't feel lighter!

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:23.910
I can do this!

00:19:23.910 --> 00:19:28.580
That player looks far sharper than she did
when I took her on in Cloudball.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:29.290
"ROOKIE EVENT SPEED SHOOTING"

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:29.290
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL - ENGINEER: TATSUYA SHIBA
PLAYERS: SUBARU SATOMI, HONOKA MITSUI"

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.170
"ROOKIE EVENT SPEED SHOOTING"
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL - ENGINEER: TATSUYA SHIBA
PLAYERS: SUBARU SATOMI, HONOKA MITSUI"

00:19:29.290 --> 00:19:31.170
Tatsuya Shiba again.

00:19:31.170 --> 00:19:33.880
It seems like the players can unleash
abilities on a different level

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:36.380
when this engineer is in charge.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:43.390
And he'll be Miyuki Shiba's engineer
for the Official Mirage Bat Event, as well.

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:47.100
Subaru also made it through the qualifying
rounds! I have to make it, too...

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:49.730
for Tatsuya's sake as my engineer!

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:52.150
And for me, this will be...

00:19:55.070 --> 00:19:56.900
Huh? She's jumping already?

00:19:56.900 --> 00:20:00.860
But there aren't any holograms yet!

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:03.740
What? The hologram showed up
where she jumped!

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:15.460
I can't get there in time
if I jump after seeing them!

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.630
How can she predict where they'll be?

00:20:17.630 --> 00:20:21.130
Now, that's what you call
showing your true abilities, yes?

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:26.600
That one can sense the light emissions
that ordinary people can ill perceive.

00:20:26.600 --> 00:20:29.430
So, Mitsui and Satomi
are both on track, huh?

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:30.390
Yes.

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:33.060
I think they'll both make the final.

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:36.940
We've finished in the top tier
in all of the Women's Rookie Events.

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:39.440
We have such a promising group
of new students this year!

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:41.570
Thank you very much.

00:20:41.570 --> 00:20:43.150
However...

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:44.610
You don't have to remind me.

00:20:44.610 --> 00:20:46.950
It's all thanks to Tatsuya, right?

00:20:46.950 --> 00:20:49.080
I have to admit,

00:20:49.080 --> 00:20:54.080
I don't know where we'd be in this year's
Nine Schools Competition without him.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:56.580
I'll have to thank him again!

00:20:58.550 --> 00:21:02.510
No matter how harsh
the Yotsuba Family is toward my brother...

00:21:02.510 --> 00:21:06.050
he can still be praised for his true value.

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:10.890
I'm so glad we enrolled
at this high school!

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.310
All right!

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:14.770
I did it, Tatsuya!

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:27.780
And now, the Monolith Code Rookie Event
between First High and Fourth High will begin!

00:21:27.780 --> 00:21:33.790
In this event, teams of three will vie
over monoliths in enemy territory using magic,

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:36.120
located on stages chosen at random!

00:21:37.000 --> 00:21:40.550
Until now, all everyone's been raving
about is how well the girls have done!

00:21:40.550 --> 00:21:42.710
Well, we're gonna win this one,
no matter what!

00:21:42.710 --> 00:21:44.220
Now that you mention it,

00:21:44.220 --> 00:21:47.890
the girls are undefeated
in all the events that Shiba worked on.

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:49.140
Are you serious?

00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.350
That's just thanks to the players' talent!

00:21:51.350 --> 00:21:56.310
Not Shiba's abilities!
No way am I ever going to acknowledge him!

00:21:56.310 --> 00:21:58.400
The event is about to start.

00:21:58.400 --> 00:22:01.360
10, 9, 8...

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:04.650
7, 6, 5...

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:06.070
4...
